<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelm Murr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1888">1888</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelm Murr was the Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauleiter">Gauleiter</a> of Württemberg-Hohenzollern and, from 1933, Reich governor of Württemberg, where he also headed the state government. He ruled the state until the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and killed himself in May 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilhelm-murr.jpg" alt="Wilhelm Murr" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gier%C5%82o%C5%BC._Gauleiters_at_Adolf_Hitler%27s_headquarters_(Wilhelm_Murr).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
